WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:09.640
In my life, I have always been
attracted to two things.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.876
One, filming videos.

00:00:11.876 --> 00:00:13.911
I would always grab the family camera

00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:17.581
and film these dramatic stories
with my little bitty toys.

00:00:18.149 --> 00:00:19.984
And on the other hand,

00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:23.521
my parents were always
making it a priority

00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:25.656
for me to learn Black history,

00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:29.660
because they knew that it wasn't going
to be a priority in my school's education.

00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:34.298
So from a very young age,
I developed the sense of voice,

00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:36.300
creativity and my message.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.069
I'm Taylor Cassidy.

00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:39.770
I’m a social media content creator

00:00:39.804 --> 00:00:41.505
and today, I want to share with you

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:45.209
why social media virality doesn’t have
the impact that you might think.

00:00:45.943 --> 00:00:48.312
So we're going to go over
to my high school years.

00:00:48.312 --> 00:00:52.817
It was 2020, and a new app
just came out, called TikTok,

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.852
and all the cool kids were getting on it.

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:57.354
And I'm a cool kid,
so I got on it as well,

00:00:57.388 --> 00:00:59.890
and I thought, "This is amazing.

00:00:59.924 --> 00:01:05.830
This is a time for me to combine
the two things that I absolutely love

00:01:05.863 --> 00:01:07.031
and put them into one."

00:01:07.064 --> 00:01:09.233
And so that's exactly what I did.

00:01:09.266 --> 00:01:12.970
Sitting on my bedroom floor
on the first day of Black History Month,

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:16.407
I created my first
Fast Black History video,

00:01:16.407 --> 00:01:20.377
where I talked about a Black figure
in 60 seconds or less,

00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:21.712
and I posted it.

00:01:21.745 --> 00:01:23.881
And it went viral, y'all. Wow.

00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:25.082
It went viral.

00:01:25.116 --> 00:01:30.254
And, I mean, thousands of people
were looking at this video

00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:31.856
and seeing this message.

00:01:31.889 --> 00:01:35.493
And I was so excited,
because the passion that I had,

00:01:35.526 --> 00:01:37.495
the passion that I had for Black history,

00:01:37.528 --> 00:01:40.131
people were loving it,
and spreading it as well.

00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:42.733
And so I continued to do it.

00:01:42.766 --> 00:01:44.835
I continued the Fast Black History series

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:48.372
and along with other videos,
I grew my account.

00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:52.076
I got 200K followers, yeah.
500K, whoo.

00:01:52.076 --> 00:01:53.711
A million followers.

00:01:53.744 --> 00:01:56.213
What? Like ... Wow.

00:01:56.247 --> 00:01:57.615
(Laughs)

00:01:57.648 --> 00:02:00.618
And when you look at these numbers,

00:02:00.618 --> 00:02:02.386
I wonder if you think to yourself,

00:02:02.419 --> 00:02:05.356
"Wow, this girl, Taylor Cassidy,
is so impressive."

00:02:05.356 --> 00:02:07.124
And I thank y'all so much.

00:02:07.124 --> 00:02:09.126
But -- (Laughs)

00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:11.595
I also want to ask you,

00:02:11.595 --> 00:02:14.465
even though you might look
at these numbers and see, like ...

00:02:14.498 --> 00:02:18.169
"Millions of people are watching her,
she must have a great impact."

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:21.505
Let me ask you,
would you think the same thing

00:02:21.539 --> 00:02:25.009
if I told you I only talked
to a thousand people a day?

00:02:25.643 --> 00:02:26.810
What about 500?

00:02:27.978 --> 00:02:29.180
What about one?

00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:34.385
Now while you think about this,
I'll take you to February of 2021.

00:02:34.418 --> 00:02:38.856
And it was one year after I started
my Fast Black History series.

00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:40.057
And I thought to myself,

00:02:40.057 --> 00:02:43.527
"Man, if that many people
looked at my videos last year,

00:02:43.561 --> 00:02:46.864
they're all going to come back, right?
I mean, probably even more so.

00:02:46.897 --> 00:02:49.033
Who wouldn't want
to support this message?"

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.868
And so I pulled out all of the stops.

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.171
I got a green screen, I got costumes,

00:02:54.205 --> 00:02:56.207
I got an external video maker.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.708
I went bougie with it.

00:02:57.741 --> 00:02:59.376
(Laughter)

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.614
And I created my first
Fast Black History video for 2021,

00:03:03.647 --> 00:03:04.782
and I posted it.

00:03:05.282 --> 00:03:07.618
And in the end,

00:03:07.651 --> 00:03:09.153
I was disappointed.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.089
I mean, where did everybody go?

00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:16.227
There weren't half as many people watching
as there were last year.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.461
What was wrong?

00:03:17.828 --> 00:03:21.565
And mind you, there were still thousands
of people watching my videos.

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:23.734
But that wasn't the problem.

00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:29.173
The problem was that my mindset
was so focused on those numbers

00:03:29.173 --> 00:03:31.742
that I thought to myself,

00:03:31.775 --> 00:03:34.845
if millions of people
weren't watching my videos,

00:03:34.845 --> 00:03:38.048
did my message even really matter
that much in the first place?

00:03:38.983 --> 00:03:43.754
And because of this,
a deep insecurity developed in me,

00:03:43.754 --> 00:03:46.824
and I started drastically
changing my content

00:03:46.824 --> 00:03:50.928
to try and adhere to trends,
to try and make it go more viral ...

00:03:51.595 --> 00:03:53.264
And, I mean, it worked.

00:03:53.297 --> 00:03:55.633
I had many viral videos after that.

00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:59.670
But why, whenever I looked at my account,

00:03:59.703 --> 00:04:02.539
why, whenever I looked at my own videos,

00:04:02.573 --> 00:04:04.241
did I not feel fulfilled?

00:04:05.743 --> 00:04:09.280
And it took this one video that I posted.

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:10.748
It was a motivational video,

00:04:10.748 --> 00:04:13.984
and, I mean, I had posted them before
and I still post them.

00:04:13.984 --> 00:04:15.219
They're so much fun.

00:04:15.252 --> 00:04:17.087
But there was this one video ...

00:04:17.388 --> 00:04:20.224
And I filmed it, posted it,

00:04:20.257 --> 00:04:21.492
and it went viral --

00:04:21.525 --> 00:04:23.794
600K views, yes.

00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:26.830
But after a while,
I privated it, I took it down.

00:04:27.965 --> 00:04:30.501
Because whenever you looked
into the comments,

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:34.238
it was only spam, random emojis

00:04:34.271 --> 00:04:36.240
and fake accounts commenting on the post.

00:04:37.207 --> 00:04:38.642
But not only this.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.646
I knew that whenever
I looked back at that video,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.984
the pep-talk sentences
that I was giving ...

00:04:47.584 --> 00:04:49.186
meant nothing to me.

00:04:49.687 --> 00:04:51.121
They weren't connected to me,

00:04:51.155 --> 00:04:54.958
and I knew that they were just buzzwords
that I was using for virality.

00:04:55.926 --> 00:04:59.363
And in the end, I didn't feel inspired.

00:05:00.964 --> 00:05:02.132
I felt sleazy.

00:05:04.034 --> 00:05:07.971
And that moment took me down
a very important and long journey

00:05:07.971 --> 00:05:11.241
of understanding
that social media virality

00:05:11.275 --> 00:05:13.811
doesn't always mean impact.

00:05:15.312 --> 00:05:16.447
2020.

00:05:17.114 --> 00:05:18.716
We had a pandemic.

00:05:18.749 --> 00:05:21.251
All of our social avenues were taken away.

00:05:21.285 --> 00:05:24.188
The way that we use our voice,
they way that we interact,

00:05:24.221 --> 00:05:25.422
was completely changed.

00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:27.891
And so we all flocked to social media.

00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:29.059
And in fact,

00:05:29.093 --> 00:05:34.498
TikTok in particular had
an 800 percent increase in users

00:05:34.498 --> 00:05:35.966
by August of 2020.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:37.801
That's crazy.

00:05:37.835 --> 00:05:40.537
That means that it's easier than ever

00:05:40.571 --> 00:05:44.108
to have millions of people
listen to what you have to say

00:05:44.141 --> 00:05:45.642
with the click of a button.

00:05:46.377 --> 00:05:48.512
But that notion,

00:05:48.512 --> 00:05:51.749
that desire for our virality,

00:05:51.749 --> 00:05:55.552
has changed the way we think
about the definition of impact.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.922
Who's a Gen Z out here? Raise your hand.

00:05:58.956 --> 00:06:00.324
Let me see y'all.

00:06:00.357 --> 00:06:01.859
Hey, I see y'all.

00:06:01.892 --> 00:06:04.661
We grew up with this notion of fame.

00:06:04.695 --> 00:06:07.931
We know what instantaneous
fame looks like.

00:06:07.965 --> 00:06:09.800
We know it, and I'll prove it to you.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.536
Look at the TV shows
that we used to watch.

00:06:12.536 --> 00:06:15.406
"Shake it Up" is about
two girls dancing ...

00:06:15.973 --> 00:06:17.508
But they're famous.

00:06:17.541 --> 00:06:20.978
"iCarly" is about a group of friends,
you know, making funny skits.

00:06:20.978 --> 00:06:22.513
But they're famous.

00:06:22.913 --> 00:06:24.148
"Hannah Montana,"

00:06:24.181 --> 00:06:26.817
this one is about just a regular girl
going to school...

00:06:29.086 --> 00:06:30.254
but she’s famous.

00:06:30.254 --> 00:06:31.622
(Laughter)

00:06:31.655 --> 00:06:33.657
And because of this --
I bring this up

00:06:33.657 --> 00:06:38.429
because we've grown up believing
that the highest point of achievement,

00:06:38.462 --> 00:06:41.532
accomplishment and impact

00:06:41.565 --> 00:06:45.369
must be achieved through fame, right?

00:06:47.037 --> 00:06:48.906
But that makes it all the more hard

00:06:48.939 --> 00:06:53.644
for somebody who doesn't have
a big following

00:06:53.677 --> 00:06:56.413
to believe that their voice
and their perspective matter,

00:06:56.447 --> 00:06:58.015
because we've grown up believing

00:06:58.048 --> 00:07:00.884
that the bigger the following,
the bigger the impact.

00:07:01.919 --> 00:07:04.188
But those two things don't add up.

00:07:04.755 --> 00:07:08.492
Or, as TikTok users would say,
"the math ain't mathing."

00:07:08.525 --> 00:07:09.726
(Laughter)

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:15.466
But what if I told you that you have
the power to change the world

00:07:15.499 --> 00:07:18.035
even if you just impact one person?

00:07:18.902 --> 00:07:21.205
I’ll show you how. Let’s get into it.

00:07:21.238 --> 00:07:25.542
Have a clear message and goal,
and then stick by it.

00:07:25.576 --> 00:07:26.743
Here's an example.

00:07:26.777 --> 00:07:32.182
This is a journal entry that I wrote
at the beginning of my TikTok career,

00:07:32.216 --> 00:07:35.786
and I basically wrote down
what TikTok meant to me,

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:39.189
what I wanted to do with it,
and what my goal was.

00:07:39.556 --> 00:07:43.260
And in doing this,
I gave myself a mission statement,

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:47.631
so that if I ever got lost
or frustrated, or confused,

00:07:47.664 --> 00:07:50.067
I had something to come back to.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:53.070
And even to this day, I come back to this

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.807
and I abide by these same themes.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.408
Now, for you, what that means

00:07:58.442 --> 00:08:01.078
is this is the part
where you cement in yourself

00:08:01.078 --> 00:08:03.814
that your perspective is needed

00:08:03.847 --> 00:08:05.449
and that it matters.

00:08:05.782 --> 00:08:09.553
And even if somebody else is doing
the same thing that you're doing,

00:08:09.586 --> 00:08:12.990
or talking about the same message
that you want to talk about,

00:08:13.023 --> 00:08:16.260
you stay steady and share it anyway,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:21.198
because your perspective
and the way that you have developed,

00:08:21.231 --> 00:08:23.500
and developed your voice in this world,

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.903
nobody else has done it like you have,

00:08:25.903 --> 00:08:27.771
and that is your superpower.

00:08:28.372 --> 00:08:31.341
Alright, we've got our message,
we're sticking by it.

00:08:31.341 --> 00:08:34.845
Now we need to check
where your resolve is placed.

00:08:35.412 --> 00:08:36.813
What is resolve?

00:08:36.847 --> 00:08:39.783
Resolve is the characteristic
that helps you to keep on going

00:08:39.783 --> 00:08:40.984
towards your goal,

00:08:41.018 --> 00:08:44.788
even when there are
inconveniences or discomforts.

00:08:44.821 --> 00:08:47.958
It's what helps you to watch
that one more Netflix episode,

00:08:47.991 --> 00:08:50.260
even though your eyes are falling asleep.

00:08:50.294 --> 00:08:53.697
It's what helps you to keep on
doing your homework, Georgetown,

00:08:53.697 --> 00:08:55.799
even when you don't feel like doing it.

00:08:55.832 --> 00:08:57.768
It's what keeps you going.

00:08:57.768 --> 00:09:00.137
And I say "check
where your resolve is placed,"

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.140
because in sharing your message or goal,

00:09:03.173 --> 00:09:06.977
it is so easy to fall into putting it

00:09:06.977 --> 00:09:09.646
into seeing how many people
you can get in front of you,

00:09:09.646 --> 00:09:12.082
seeing how many people you can reach.

00:09:12.115 --> 00:09:14.851
And in doing that,
you sacrifice your message

00:09:14.851 --> 00:09:17.454
and exploit it for fame and popularity.

00:09:18.822 --> 00:09:21.825
Instead, place your resolve in knowing

00:09:21.825 --> 00:09:26.129
that you have the very ability
to impact one person

00:09:26.163 --> 00:09:27.598
and change their life,

00:09:27.631 --> 00:09:31.668
because you have the ability
to change the world ...

00:09:32.502 --> 00:09:36.139
But you also have the ability
to impact one person

00:09:36.173 --> 00:09:39.176
who has the ability
to change the world as well.

00:09:39.176 --> 00:09:41.778
And that is still so cool.

00:09:42.446 --> 00:09:47.351
OK, you may be thinking,
"Taylor, alright, I've got my message,

00:09:47.384 --> 00:09:50.721
I'm sticking by it,
I know where my resolve is placed.

00:09:50.754 --> 00:09:54.458
So why in the world,
whenever I post a video on Instagram,

00:09:54.491 --> 00:09:56.426
it doesn't even get 10 likes?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.295
Why is that?"

00:09:58.862 --> 00:10:00.130
And I'll tell you,

00:10:00.163 --> 00:10:04.167
even though there might not be
millions of people looking at your video,

00:10:04.201 --> 00:10:07.771
you really don’t know
who is going to stop on it

00:10:07.804 --> 00:10:11.441
and truly take to heart
the words that you have to say.

00:10:12.142 --> 00:10:14.277
And that brings me to my last point.

00:10:14.311 --> 00:10:17.014
Focus on the impact of one.

00:10:17.047 --> 00:10:19.516
You see my transition? Yeah.

00:10:19.549 --> 00:10:22.619
I’ll give you more examples. 
You know I come with the receipts.

00:10:22.953 --> 00:10:27.391
These comments
are from videos that I posted,

00:10:27.391 --> 00:10:29.626
where somebody was inspired by them

00:10:29.626 --> 00:10:33.964
or inspired by my account to go out
and make a change in their own life.

00:10:33.964 --> 00:10:37.367
And one of them even says
that they are going into their school

00:10:37.401 --> 00:10:40.303
and campaigning for more
Black history to be taught,

00:10:40.303 --> 00:10:44.541
the very message that I wanted
to share in the first place.

00:10:44.574 --> 00:10:47.144
And I show you
these specific comments

00:10:47.177 --> 00:10:49.212
because every single one of them

00:10:49.246 --> 00:10:54.451
came from videos that a lot of people
consider flopped --

00:10:54.451 --> 00:10:57.354
did not go viral, "unsuccessful," failed.

00:10:58.321 --> 00:11:01.858
But that goes to show
that the videos that I posted

00:11:01.892 --> 00:11:06.897
weren’t defined by the millions of people
that did or didn’t look at them.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.499
They were defined
by the very ability that they had

00:11:09.533 --> 00:11:12.102
to reach out and impact one person

00:11:12.102 --> 00:11:14.771
to go and change their entire community.

00:11:14.805 --> 00:11:19.409
And that is so much more
valuable and sustaining

00:11:19.443 --> 00:11:21.578
than creating something
or sharing something

00:11:21.611 --> 00:11:24.548
just for the purpose
of getting quick virality.

00:11:26.516 --> 00:11:27.684
Alright.

00:11:27.718 --> 00:11:29.019
We've got our message,

00:11:29.052 --> 00:11:30.620
we've got our understanding

00:11:30.654 --> 00:11:33.523
that the individual impact
is just as important

00:11:33.557 --> 00:11:35.659
as reaching a thousand.

00:11:35.659 --> 00:11:40.697
So why is it so hard for us to share
our perspective and our voice?

00:11:40.731 --> 00:11:43.934
How is it so hard for us
to get over that fear?

00:11:44.968 --> 00:11:46.937
I'll tell you one more story before I go.

00:11:47.571 --> 00:11:51.341
[When] I was in high school,
I entered a short film competition

00:11:51.374 --> 00:11:54.978
where I made a short film
about a young Black girl

00:11:55.011 --> 00:11:59.249
going through school and finding
her own identity as a Black woman

00:11:59.282 --> 00:12:01.485
in the midst of stereotypes
being pushed on her

00:12:01.518 --> 00:12:03.920
by her peers and her classmates.

00:12:04.354 --> 00:12:09.226
And in doing this, I was so scared,

00:12:09.226 --> 00:12:13.497
because it was a story
that I had went through,

00:12:13.497 --> 00:12:15.766
was a very personal story of mine,

00:12:15.799 --> 00:12:17.033
but I pushed on anyway.

00:12:17.067 --> 00:12:18.769
Here are some stills from the film.

00:12:18.802 --> 00:12:21.505
“Oh my gosh, Hayley Cassidy
is just like Issa Rae.”

00:12:21.505 --> 00:12:22.539
Wow!

00:12:22.539 --> 00:12:24.574
Thank you, I appreciate it.

00:12:24.608 --> 00:12:28.612
But I was so scared to make this film,
but I pushed on anyway.

00:12:28.645 --> 00:12:29.913
And at the film festival,

00:12:29.946 --> 00:12:32.816
[when] they were showing
all of the competitors’ films,

00:12:32.849 --> 00:12:35.585
afterwards, a girl came up to me,

00:12:35.619 --> 00:12:40.090
and basically said to me how much
she related with the main character,

00:12:40.123 --> 00:12:43.760
how much she understood
what the main character went through,

00:12:43.794 --> 00:12:47.164
and she thanked me for making
something that connected with her

00:12:47.164 --> 00:12:49.032
and helped her to feel seen.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.335
And in that moment,

00:12:52.369 --> 00:12:55.238
I understood something
very, very important.

00:12:56.573 --> 00:13:01.711
If I had let my fear of embarrassment,
my fear of failure,

00:13:01.745 --> 00:13:04.414
or my fear of lack
of a reaction from people,

00:13:04.447 --> 00:13:07.551
stop me from spreading this message,

00:13:07.551 --> 00:13:08.919
I would have never been able

00:13:08.952 --> 00:13:12.322
to give someone the permission
to let go of their own fear.

00:13:13.323 --> 00:13:14.691
For you,

00:13:14.691 --> 00:13:18.695
what that means is that the passion,
the urgency and the love

00:13:18.728 --> 00:13:21.998
that you have for your idea
and your message

00:13:22.032 --> 00:13:24.434
must be greater than your fear.

00:13:25.268 --> 00:13:27.938
And notice how I said "greater than,"

00:13:27.971 --> 00:13:29.906
and not that fear will be nonexistent.

00:13:30.907 --> 00:13:33.243
Because the very fact
that fear and anxiety

00:13:33.243 --> 00:13:35.011
are associated with your message

00:13:35.045 --> 00:13:39.482
is proof that it has the power
to change everything.

00:13:40.784 --> 00:13:41.918
So,

00:13:42.319 --> 00:13:45.188
as you go on into your life,

00:13:45.188 --> 00:13:46.790
maybe you'll go into business,

00:13:46.823 --> 00:13:48.358
maybe you'll go into art.

00:13:48.391 --> 00:13:51.761
Maybe you'll become
a Twitch streamer, I don't know.

00:13:51.795 --> 00:13:53.797
They make a lot of good money.

00:13:54.531 --> 00:13:57.200
Remember to keep steady in your message.

00:13:57.667 --> 00:14:03.807
Protect your voice from being distorted
by gaining popularity and fame,

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.844
and understand and focus
on the individual impact of one.

00:14:08.712 --> 00:14:10.580
Know that your perspective,

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:14.251
the way you act
and interact in this world,

00:14:14.284 --> 00:14:16.219
is the key to changing it.

00:14:17.087 --> 00:14:18.455
I believe in you.

00:14:18.922 --> 00:14:20.056
Keep rising.

00:14:20.557 --> 00:14:21.825
Thank you so much.

